<title>BELGIUM: EU clears Merck, Roche AIDS drugs.</title>
<headline>EU clears Merck, Roche AIDS drugs.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had approved the marketing in the European Union of two AIDS (Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome) drugs produced by Merck &amp; Co. and Roche Holding Limited.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Commission said the drugs are Merck's Crixivan and Roche's Invirase.</p>
<p>He said EU national experts had given their approval for the marketing of the two drugs after a positive opinion from the London-based European drugs agency EMEA. -- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
